::MLA.ENG1.C.01 U06 L06 GP Q01::
MLA Standard: MLA.ENG1.C.01
Slide note: Revision improves clarity. Which speaker note best supports the slide? {
~A. Revision improves clarity because the slide says it does.#Incorrect. This only repeats the slide without adding explanation.
~B. Revision is a word on this slide.#Incorrect. This does not explain the meaning of the slide.
=C. Revision helps writers make ideas easier to follow by improving word choice, transitions, and explanations.#Correct. This speaker note explains the slide instead of simply repeating it.
~D. I will read the slide now.#Incorrect. Reading the slide aloud does not add meaningful oral explanation.
}

::MLA.ENG1.C.02 U06 L06 GP Q02::
MLA Standard: MLA.ENG1.C.02
Which slide note is best for an integrated oral and digital presentation? {
~A. A long paragraph with every planned sentence#Incorrect. Slides should not carry the whole speech.
=B. Feedback reveals unclear claims.#Correct. Review the lesson explanation to confirm why this choice fits or does not fit.
~C. Stuff about feedback and writing#Incorrect. This is too vague to guide the audience.
~D. I will say something here.#Incorrect. This does not communicate a useful idea.
}

::MLA.ENG1.V.03 U06 L06 GP Q03::
MLA Standard: MLA.ENG1.C.03
In a presentation, the word "credible" means which of the following? {
~A. confusing and unsupported#Incorrect. Credible information should be clear and supported.
=B. trustworthy and reliable#Correct. In this context, credible evidence is evidence the audience can trust.
~C. colorful and decorative#Incorrect. Color and decoration do not determine credibility.
~D. unrelated but interesting#Incorrect. Interesting information is not necessarily credible or relevant.
}

::MLA.ENG1.L.01 U06 L06 GP Q04::
MLA Standard: MLA.ENG1.L.01
Which slide note uses standard English conventions? {
~A. Revision help writers make ideas clearer.#Incorrect. The verb does not agree with the singular subject "Revision."
~B. Revision help writer's make ideas clear.#Incorrect. This has agreement and apostrophe errors.
~C. Revision helping writers make ideas clearer.#Incorrect. This is a fragment rather than a complete sentence.
=D. Revision helps writers make ideas clearer.#Correct. The sentence uses correct subject-verb agreement.
}

::MLA.ENG1.C.03 U06 L06 GP Q05::
MLA Standard: MLA.ENG1.V.03
Before sharing a collaborative digital presentation, what should students check? {
=A. Whether the presentation is polished, audience-aware, and ready to share#Correct. This matches publication-ready communication for a specific audience.
~B. Whether every slide has the most words possible#Incorrect. Publication-ready work should be clear, not overcrowded.
~C. Whether the presentation uses random formatting#Incorrect. Random formatting weakens publication-ready quality.
~D. Whether speaker notes and slides are unrelated#Incorrect. Integrated communication requires connection between slides and oral explanation.
}
